# Reviewed divergences between the pinned oracle and ztsc.
#
# `.expected` snapshots are pure oracle output and are never hand-edited, so
# `node test/conformance/gen_expected.js test/conformance --check` is a real
# gate. Every deliberate difference is recorded here instead, one per line:
#
#   <case-path>  -TS<code> [<file>] <line>   oracle reports it, ztsc does not
#   <case-path>  +TS<code> [<file>] <line>   ztsc reports it, the oracle does not
#
# (`<file>` only for directory cases, matching the snapshot format.)
#
# Policy: a missed error (`-`) is acceptable when it is deterministic and
# reasoned; a false positive is not. A `+` entry therefore needs a stronger
# justification than a `-` entry and is only defensible when the same
# diagnostic is also present in the snapshot at a different span.
#
# The registry is self-cleaning: run_conformance.zig fails the case if an entry
# stops describing reality (ztsc started emitting a `-` line, stopped emitting
# a `+` line, the oracle dropped a `-` line, or the case is gone). It cannot be
# used to hide a regression.
#
# What the registry cannot check is whether an entry's REASON is still true, so
# every block below carries the date its rationale was last measured against
# the oracle. Full triage: 2026-08-02 (B4). Every remaining entry is a
# deliberate under-report whose alternative was measured to cost more than it
# buys — a false positive on correct code in every case where the alternative
# was reachable enough to measure.

# TS2589 at a recursion cap. ztsc's caps assume the relation and stay silent
# rather than reporting where they cut. They are RESOURCE bounds, not semantic
# ones — `max_relation_depth`, `max_chain_repeats` and (since B1)
# `max_relation_identity_repeats`, all in `src/checker.zig` — and their shape
# is not tsc's `instantiationDepth`/`instantiationCount` budget, so a report at
# ztsc's cut fires on inputs tsc accepts. Assuming the relation is the only
# direction at a resource bound that cannot manufacture a false positive; the
# cases exist to prove these inputs keep checking, deterministically, without
# stack-overflowing.
#
# How reachable the caps are, measured 2026-08-02 by flipping the
# `max_relation_depth` cut's answer from "related" to "unrelated" and diffing:
# exactly ONE conformance case changes (003, the case built to trip it), and
# nothing changes on the 16-package corpus or on excalidraw.
# So the caps are nowhere near live code today — which is the argument for
# leaving them silent, not against it. See the comment in each case file.
instantiation/003_recursive_alias_relation_cap.ts  -TS2589 19
instantiation/010_growing_bareref_no_eager_expand.ts  -TS2589 12

