# suppression half of `@ts-expect-error` is; the unused report is not, because
# it is only sound on a checker that reports everything the oracle does: it
# fires precisely when a directive suppressed nothing, so it is built on
# ztsc's own report set rather than on the oracle's.
#
# Re-examined 2026-08-02, after under-reports reached zero on all eight parity
# packages and on excalidraw. Zero *there* is not zero: every remaining entry
# in this file is a line where the oracle considers a directive used and ztsc
# would consider it unused — a numeric-literal key (`constassert/006`), a cast
# through a deferred `T[K]` (`indexed/032`), a callback-parameter direction
# (`assignability/065`), TS2589 at a recursion cap (`instantiation/003`, `010`,
# `018`), a still-deferred type argument (`instantiation/052`). TS2578 on that
# basis is a false positive on correct code — the one thing project policy
# forbids — so the prerequisite is unchanged: this file empty of `-` entries,
# not a clean scoreboard on one corpus.
#
# `directives/013_ts_expect_error_over_under_report.ts` makes that concrete
# and executable: two directives over diagnostics ztsc deliberately does not
# make, where the oracle reports nothing and so must ztsc. Implement TS2578
# before closing those under-reports and that case fails with a `+TS2578`.
#
# Deterministic under-report of a whole check.
directives/012_ts_expect_error_unused.ts  -TS2578 7

# The callback-parameter relation is ADDITIVE in ztsc, where tsc makes it the
# only test for a pair of single-call-signature parameters. When the callback
# comparison fails, ztsc falls back to the pre-existing
# contravariant/bivariant parameter check instead of rejecting, so the two
# directions tsc rejects *because* the callback relation is exclusive are
# under-reported: a method callback related in the contravariant direction
# (line 25), and a callback nested one level deeper, which tsc relates
# strictly (line 74).
#
# Re-measured 2026-08-02, after the B1 relation work (memo-key
# canonicalization, the growing-instantiation guard, measured variance) — the
# fixes that were the standing reason to re-evaluate. Making the rule
# exclusive (the fall-through below `signatureAssignableMode`'s callback arm
# replaced by `return false`) does fix exactly these two lines and regresses
# no other conformance case, but it still costs more than it buys: on the
# 16-package corpus it is byte-identical on fifteen packages and adds TEN new
# false positives on rxjs 7.8.1 —
#
#   Notification.ts:180, concatWith.ts:47, delayWhen.ts:98, elementAt.ts:62,
#   first.ts:86, ignoreElements.ts:42, last.ts:84, mergeWith.ts:48,
#   onErrorResumeNextWith.ts:93 (TS2322) and catchError.ts:117 (TS2345)
#
# — every one of them the same unrelated inference gap the exclusivity merely
# surfaces: ztsc infers `Observable<unknown>` / `OperatorFunction<…, unknown>`
# where tsc infers the element type. The prerequisite is that inference gap,
# not the relation. The 7 positives in the same case prove the callback
# relation itself is in place.
assignability/065_callback_parameter_variance.ts  -TS2322 25
assignability/065_callback_parameter_variance.ts  -TS2322 74

# A cast whose source or target is a DEFERRED indexed access (`T[K]`) is
